# F48. Someone keeps a small Notes window. It spends an hour as a column, and when it floats
# again it is small again. "Float All Windows" and pausing put everything back as it was.
# As the first build shipped it: docked windows are dragged out onto the Desktop beside others.
set desktopColumn true
quiet
open Notes 400x300
open Safari 800x600
open Mail 640x420

dock 101 left
dock 102 right
expect docked 101
float 101
expect floating 101
expect size 101 400x300
expect visible 101

# Framed, it fills the display. Floated from there it is small again, and the Desktop is in view.
dock 101 left
zoom 101
expect fills 101
float 101
expect size 101 400x300
expect visible 101
expect visible 103

# Dragged out of its slot and dropped on the Desktop.
dock 101 left
drag 101 720 300 cmd
expect floating 101
expect size 101 400x300

# Arrange leaves only a narrow Desktop. A window floated from there still has its own size, over the docked
# windows if need be, and so has one that is dragged out: the two ways to float agree.
arrange
float 102
expect size 102 800x600
expect visible 102
arrange
drag 102 1300 300 cmd
expect floating 102
expect size 102 800x600
expect visible 102

# Floated out of a view without the Desktop, it belongs to that view: walk away, come back, and it is there.
open Slack
arrange
zoom 101
out
float 101
expect visible 101
neighbor right
expect hidden 101
back
expect visible 101
expect size 101 400x300
close 104

# Walking a docked window about changes nothing.
arrange
expect count docked 3
dock 101 right
dock 101 down
dock 101 left
zoom 102
float-all
expect count docked 0
expect size 101 400x300
expect size 102 800x600
expect size 103 640x420

# Framed on Safari, a pause lets go as a quit would: Safari has its own size again, and the windows that were out
# of view come back on screen at theirs. Resuming takes them back.
arrange
zoom 102
expect fills 102
pause
expect size 102 800x600
expect visible 101
expect size 101 400x300
expect size 103 640x420
resume
expect fills 102
expect hidden 101
expect count docked 3

# There and back is nothing. Docked by a key and floated again, Notes is where it was, not only as large as it was,
# whichever way it leaves, and though Safari stays docked under it. Named while Safari is worked in, it comes to the front.
float-all
move 101 800 300 400 300
dock 102 right
dock 101 left
focus 102
toggle-float 101
expect at 101 800 300 400x300
expect docked 102
expect focused 101
expect in-front 101
dock 101 left
dock 101 right
float 101
expect at 101 800 300 400x300
dock 101 left
float-all
expect at 101 800 300 400x300
dock 101 left
pause
expect at 101 800 300 400x300
resume

# Pushed aside by hand until a strip shows, it goes back to its strip.
float-all
move 101 1340 300 400 300
dock 101 left
float 101
expect at 101 1340 300 400x300
dock 101 left
pause
expect at 101 1340 300 400x300
resume
